+**A dependency-light source profile and Rust conformance surface for
+Full-owned GKX contracts.**
+
+GKOS-Engine-Lite is not a second knowledge engine. GKOS-Engine Full remains the
+TypeScript contract and reference-semantics authority. Lite's current Node
+wrapper delegates an allowed command surface to an exact Full dependency; its
+Rust workspace privately verifies selected Full-produced contracts. Lite does
+not independently parse GKX, define identity or lineage, activate a watcher,
+host MCP, or obtain filesystem-effects authority.
+
+## Capability and release status
+
+The three status classes below must not be collapsed.
+
+| Surface | Status | Exact boundary |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Current source checkout | Legacy Node wrapper; not a registry-install claim | Restricted command delegation, optional proposal-only assistance client, and desktop presentation source. No claim is made that `gkos-engine-lite` is published on npm. |
+| Functional uplift Phases 0-5 | Draft-qualified, verifier-only/stacked | Lite implementation `6d94e40dc11e1bb43693b225e32ec6110d4e03b1`, run `32807434279`; evidence head `a39f14d1394e3dd8f8dada8bec77bd995b1a0bc4`, run `32808011926`; draft PR #20. Full authority is `7b5262baee9fcda23d50b0cee0c4977d6e4305e7`. |
+| Functional uplift Phases 6-11 | Future planned work | Public watcher runtime, authenticated multi-agent MCP, graph tools, UI integration, packaging, final documentation, and cross-repository handoff are not implemented or released. |
+
+The Phase 5 Rust watcher component is crate-private and inert. It verifies the
+copied Full pack and fixture semantics; it is not a public watcher service,
+filesystem writer, executable, or service activation. The current sidecar is
+an authenticated, GET-only loopback REST surface with `/health`, `/notes`,
+`/graph`, and `/graphiti/episodes`. It has no `/mcp` route. The desktop's MCP
+snippets therefore do not describe a working endpoint at this coordinate.
+
+## Authority allocation
+
+- `gkos-standard` owns normative GKOS/GKX meaning.
+- Full owns the TypeScript parser, deterministic semantics, contract packs,
+  reference behavior, and operational host decisions.
+- Lite consumes exact Full pins. Rust may prove cross-language conformance but
+  may not create a second parser, lineage model, authority system, or denial
+  semantics.
+- The wrapper, desktop shell, optional models, and future transports are
+  presentation or adapter layers only.
+
+## Sensitivity and access-control boundary
+
+`sensitivity` is projection metadata, not access control. The current `/notes`
+and `/graph` routes return all indexed records and attach sensitivity metadata;
+`default_sensitivity` does not enforce a visibility ceiling. Authentication of
+the loopback transport does not provide per-agent identity or authorization.
+Any host that discloses results must separately authenticate the caller and
+enforce its discoverability policy before returning records.
+
+## Current and draft functionality
+
+From a source checkout, the current wrapper can delegate its allowed commands
+to the pinned Full engine. The optional `assist` client sends proposal-only
+requests to a separately configured loopback intelligence service and does not
+apply source changes.
+
+On the draft uplift stack, Rust remains a private conformance/verifier layer:
+
+- Phase 1 verifies deterministic retrieval-contract behavior.
+- Phase 2 verifies citation and temporal coordinates.
+- Phase 3 verifies ingest and sealed-generation contracts while Full remains
+  parser, storage-owner, and activation authority.
+- Phase 4 verifies evaluation/tuning envelopes and delegates the CLI to Full.
+- Phase 5 verifies the exact watcher/recovery pack without exposing runtime
+  watcher or effects authority.
+
+No npm publication, final `gkx-lite` executable, signed installer, operational
+MCP endpoint, governed external-effects plane, or activated Phase 5 watcher is
+claimed.
+
+## Future planned sequence
+
+After Full defects are repaired and independently qualified, future phases may
+add identity-bound MCP, bounded graph projections/tools, truthful operator
+interfaces, clean-machine packaging, final documentation, and integration.
+Each Lite step follows a hosted-green Full contract pin and reciprocal review.
+Planning does not authorize merge, tag, release, publication, deployment,
+service activation, or external effects.
 
 ## Why "Lite"
 
-The full [gkos-engine](https://github.com/Odenknight/GKOS-Engine) can read
